markdown <<MARKDOWN
#Begin with the End in Mind: Final Project Overview

#### Let's take a moment to begin with the end in mind by taking a look at the Final Project for this Unit.

## Interactive Customizer

#### In this project, students take on the role of Front-End Developers and QA Engineers to design and implement a badge-awarding system in a web app of their choice (sports, music, art, gaming, school life, and more).

<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;"> <div> <h4 style="margin-top: 0; font-weight: bold">Students will:</h4> <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt"> <li>Design a custom badge system with clearly defined achievement criteria.</li> <br> <li>Create a flowchart to plan the logic behind their badge-awarding system.</li> <br> <li>Translate their plan into JavaScript using functions, variables, and conditionals.</li> <br> <li>Build a dynamic interface that updates based on user actions.</li> <br> <li>Test and refine their code while documenting their debugging process.</li> <br> <li>Reflect on how AI supported their brainstorming and problem-solving.</li> </ul> </div> <div> <img src="https://images.code.org/4e1b6412c687590c048f087cef0675e6-image-1741789708762.png" alt="Icon of clipboard and pen" style="border-radius: 10px; width: 200px; height: auto;"> </div> </div>

####The result is a personalized, interactive app that demonstrates how developer choices and values shape user experience.
 

---

### **When Project Begins:** Final lesson of the unit

### The project extends over three class periods. Beginning in Lesson 11.

## Sample

#### In this early example, the student designed a web app to order an ultimate burrito bowl. 

#### This is the initial output based on the wireframe uploaded by the student. 


<img src="https://images.code.org/18c2321f0c5f2626200d4c872239ac1c-image-1771608745433.png" alt="Sample student project of a website for ordering food from a burrito bowl websit" width="850px" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; border: 3pt solid black; box-shadow: 5px 5px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.4); border-radius: 2px;">

---


## What Success Looks Like

#### This project lets students apply their design and coding skills in a creative, authentic way while demonstrating clear logic, strong programming practices, and thoughtful iteration.

<div style="display:flex; justify-content:center; gap:16px; flex-wrap:wrap;"> <div style="background:#f2f2f2; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.15); border-radius:8px; padding:16px 20px; text-align:center; width:170px; font-size:14pt;"> <span style="display:block; font-size:28pt; margin-bottom:8px;">🗺️</span> Flowchart logic aligns clearly with JavaScript implementation </div> <div style="background:#f2f2f2; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.15); border-radius:8px; padding:16px 20px; text-align:center; width:170px; font-size:14pt;"> <span style="display:block; font-size:28pt; margin-bottom:8px;">🏷️</span> Badges awarded deterministically based on user input </div> <div style="background:#f2f2f2; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.15); border-radius:8px; padding:16px 20px; text-align:center; width:170px; font-size:14pt;"> <span style="display:block; font-size:28pt; margin-bottom:8px;">🔢</span> Variables track selections and calculated values (ex: total price) </div> <div style="background:#f2f2f2; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.15); border-radius:8px; padding:16px 20px; text-align:center; width:170px; font-size:14pt;"> <span style="display:block; font-size:28pt; margin-bottom:8px;">🧩</span> Organized, readable functions with accurate UI updates </div> <div style="background:#f2f2f2; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.15); border-radius:8px; padding:16px 20px; text-align:center; width:170px; font-size:14pt;"> <span style="display:block; font-size:28pt; margin-bottom:8px;">🔍</span> Clear evidence of testing, debugging, and iteration </div> </div>

## Now, let’s see how we get here! 

